{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971118-the-wicked-30-gmc-from-the-80s-to-the-00s","id":971118,"title":"The Wicked 30: GMC from the 80s to the 00s","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T20:45:14-07:00","id":971118,"title":"The Wicked 30: GMC from the 80s to the 00s","content":"So, conversation in the Dark Eras 2 thread led to us discussing some pretty recent Dark Eras, and I proposed that there's actually quite a lot to be done with the last few decades, the birth of the Internet combined with the turn of the millennium. <br /> <br /> I admit, this is shamelessly inspired by tumblr aesthetic bloggers and their talent for turning the cultural detritus of the 90s and 00s into a nightmarish cyberpunk mindscape. <br /> <br /> So: I want this thread to be a repository for the weirdest things you can think about from living in the 80s, 90s, or 00s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:08:28-07:00","id":971327,"title":"","content":"The console wars of the 90s introduced many children to the idea of sectarian warfare based on group identity before many of them were old enough to really understand the religions their parents followed. I can't help but love the idea of the whole thing being a MG experiment in group identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:45:56-07:00","id":971337,"title":"","content":"There were a number of media experiences on tele that exploded in the decades of the '80s and '90s, all of them things that we now take for granted. A few examples are:<br /> <br /> Cable Television (Channel 6 in the UK) \u2013 'What? I don't just gotta watch what the networks offer anymore? No way!' <br /> Music Videos \u2013 Even a whole network (on the cable, above) for them! Note: It didn't last, but we can lament MTV another time.<br /> Twenty-four Hour News Cycles \u2013 Okay, this one does still get mentioned, but until it is, we tend to assume it's the way things ought to be, yeah?<br /> 'Reality Teevee' \u2013 We've always had this, sure, but now it's all over, all the time, all celebs doing it, to a point where lines between DIY, gossip, and voyeurism blur.<br /> <br /> ...I know that there are more, but these are the ones that came to mind straight away and we don't really bat an eye at them like we should do. That last one, in fact, ought to scare us since it's EXACTLY what Ray Bradbury suggested would lead to the death of literature in <i>Fahrenheit 451</i> decades before it became real! <br /> <br /> Surely the God-Machine had it's angels doing some of this, though one wonders what outcome such Infrastructure was meant to create...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:50:37-07:00","id":971339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971118-the-wicked-30-gmc-from-the-80s-to-the-00s?p=971327#post971327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The console wars of the 90s...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, mate! This is STILL a war that goes on, but by the 2000s it became so entrenched as to reach more a status of being Console Cold War with three big players \u2013 alas poor Sega, we hardly knew ye!<br /> <br /> The REAL war should be between consoles and PCs, but somehow that line has not flared into open hostilities. Wonder why? The God-Machine will win either way, so It won't waste resources on this... Or maybe we just cannot SEE the war's battlefields. <br /> <br /> Yikes, it gives me shivers to think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:21:24-07:00","id":971418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971118-the-wicked-30-gmc-from-the-80s-to-the-00s?p=971339#post971339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, mate! This is STILL a war that goes on, but by the 2000s it became so entrenched as to reach more a status of being Console Cold War with three big players \u2013 alas poor Sega, we hardly knew ye!<br /> <br /> The REAL war should be between consoles and PCs, but somehow that line has not flared into open hostilities. Wonder why? The God-Machine will win either way, so It won't waste resources on this... Or maybe we just cannot SEE the war's battlefields.<br /> <br /> Yikes, it gives me shivers to think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just finished reading that book on the 90s console wars by Blake Harris (it was at my local library of all places). It's no wonder they are turning it into a movie, the behind the scenes stuff involved in Sega's rapid rise and fall is pure Hollywood drama, though one could argue that the book has some biases, especially regarding which branch of Sega was responsible for it's downfall. Also the great comics crash of 1996 lead directly to Magic the Gathering via marvel's deal with wizards of the coast to make trading cards packaged with their comics, amoung other long term effects on nerd culture, perhaps someone planned for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:07:47-07:00","id":971517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971118-the-wicked-30-gmc-from-the-80s-to-the-00s?p=971418#post971418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the great comics crash of 1996 lead directly to Magic the Gathering via marvel's deal with wizards of the coast to make trading cards packaged with their comics, amoung other long term effects on nerd culture, perhaps someone planned for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>:/ Magic the Gathering was first published in 1993.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:28:52-07:00","id":971540,"title":"","content":"Honest having lived through the ninities at the time I found it boring.<br /> <br /> In hind sight it was the golden age of Star Trek TNG, DS9, Voy. This was the era that made me a Trekkie. The Original Series was foundational, but without TNG, DS9, and Voy it would have remained a mild curiousity.<br /> <br /> Several Star Trek Movies were done in the 90\u2019s as well.<br /> <br /> I loved Angel and Buffy series as well.<br /> <br /> At the time I felt the music was inferior to the 80\u2018s, but while the 80\u2019s music still holds primaricy, there was SOME good music that I liked in the 90's.<br /> <br /> 90210 and Melrose Place I enjoyed.<br /> <br /> Ontario my province was the setting for extremely different provincial governments, the NDPs Bob Ray government, the one and only NDP government in Ontario history, and then the Neoliberal Tory government of Mike Harris.<br /> <br /> On a personal level I believe it was the 90\u2019s were arrogance turned into self hatred and depression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:47:12-07:00","id":971549,"title":"","content":"I do remember the early internet and BBS of the 90s. What we curreny have tech wise is so much better now.<br /> <br /> Early 2000\u2018s from 2000 to 2010 my mom died and that caused alot of choas in my life.<br /> <br /> The rise of Jack Layton within the NDP.<br /> <br /> The eventually beginnings of THE AGE OF FREE PORN, which causes disarray in the porn industry, and great joy in the young and broke males (and some female).<br /> <br /> Stargate SG-1, Stargate Altantis, Lost Girl, Smallville, 2 and a Half Men.<br /> <br /> In Canada the end of the Federal Liberal Dynasty and the beginning of a series of minority governments begins (or to me what I'd call the good old days of politics when things felt hopeful and anything was possible, which ended when we elected Prime Minister Selfie and the so called natural governing party recaptured power.<br /> <br /> For me personally a time of confusion and bitter disappoints with a couple of good bright spots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:49:19-07:00","id":971550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971118-the-wicked-30-gmc-from-the-80s-to-the-00s?p=971517#post971517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:/ Magic the Gathering was first published in 1993.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but marvel made the deal with wizards that gave them the resources needed to make magic before that, it's just that the deal was bas for marvel and contributed to the comics crash years later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/ava